block head
    title Gingivitis - Plants Cause Disease

block content
    h1 Gingivitis
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/gingivitis/symptoms-causes/syc-20354453") Mayo Clinic]:
    blockquote Gingivitis is a common and mild form of gum disease (periodontal disease) that causes irritation, redness and swelling (inflammation) of your gingiva, the part of your gum around the base of your teeth. It's important to take gingivitis seriously and treat it promptly. Gingivitis can lead to much more serious gum disease called periodontitis and tooth loss.
